# Rapport d'Architecture – TalentFlow  

## 1. Setup & Stack Technique  
**Frontend** :  
- React.js (TypeScript)  
- React Router v6  
- Material UI v5  
- Axios (API client)  
- JWT (Authentification)  
- WebSockets (Messagerie temps réel)  
- Chart.js (Graphiques Analytics)  

**Backend** :  
- Node.js (v18+)  
- NestJS (Framework MVC)  
- PostgreSQL (ORM: TypeORM)  
- Redis (Cache/Sessions)  
- JWT (Authentification)  
- Socket.IO (WebSocket)  
- BullMQ (File d’attente pour notifications)  

**BDD** :  
- PostgreSQL 14  
- Tables principales : `users`, `companies`, `jobs`, `candidates`, `applications`, `interviews`, `evaluations`, `skills`, `notifications`, `activity_logs`  

**Déploiement/DevOps** :  
- Docker (Conteneurisation)  
- Kubernetes (Orchestration)  
- GitHub Actions (CI/CD)  
- Nginx (Reverse Proxy)  
- Let’s Encrypt (SSL)  
- AWS S3 (Stockage fichiers)  
- AWS RDS (Base de données)  

---

## 2. Schéma Relationnel de la Base de Données  
**Entités principales** :  
- **Users** : `user_id` (PK), `email`, `password_hash`, `role_id` (FK → Roles), `created_at`  
- **Roles** : `role_id` (PK), `name` (Admin, Recruiter, Hiring Manager, Candidate)  
- **Companies** : `company_id` (PK), `name`, `industry`, `location`, `created_at`  
- **Jobs** : `job_id` (PK), `title`, `department`, `location`, `work_mode`, `status` (Active/Closed), `company_id` (FK), `created_at`  
- **Candidates** : `candidate_id` (PK), `user_id` (FK → Users), `resume_url`, `score`, `created_at`  
- **Applications** : `application_id` (PK), `job_id` (FK → Jobs), `candidate_id` (FK → Candidates), `status` (Applied/Screening/Shortlisted/Interview/Offer/Hired/Rejected), `created_at`  
- **Interviews** : `interview_id` (PK), `application_id` (FK → Applications), `scheduled_at`, `duration`, `type` (Technical/Phone/Video), `meeting_link`, `created_at`  
- **Evaluations** : `evaluation_id` (PK), `interview_id` (FK → Interviews), `interviewer_id` (FK → Users), `technical_skills` (1-5), `communication` (1-5), `problem_solving` (1-5), `culture_fit` (1-5), `recommendation` (Strong Hire/Hire/Maybe/No Hire), `comments`, `created_at`  
- **Skills** : `skill_id` (PK), `name` (ex: Python, React)  
- **Candidate_Skills** : `candidate_id` (FK → Candidates), `skill_id` (FK → Skills) (Relation N-N)  
- **Notifications** : `notification_id` (PK), `user_id` (FK → Users), `message`, `is_read`, `created_at`  
- **Activity_Logs** : `log_id` (PK), `user_id` (FK → Users), `action` (ex: "Moved candidate to Interview"), `candidate_id` (FK → Candidates), `timestamp`  

**Relations** :  
- `Users` → `Roles` (1-N)  
- `Companies` → `Jobs` (1-N)  
- `Jobs` → `Applications` (1-N)  
- `Candidates` → `Applications` (1-N)  
- `Applications` → `Interviews` (1-N)  
- `Interviews` → `Evaluations` (1-N)  
- `Candidates` ↔ `Skills` (N-N via `Candidate_Skills`)  
- `Users` → `Notifications` (1-N)  
- `Users` → `Activity_Logs` (1-N)  

---

## 3. Architecture Backend & APIs  
**API REST principales** :  
- `/auth` (Login, Register, JWT Refresh)  
- `/users` (Gestion utilisateurs, rôles)  
- `/companies` (CRUD entreprises)  
- `/jobs` (CRUD offres, recherche/filtres)  
- `/candidates` (Gestion candidats, compétences)  
- `/applications` (Pipeline candidature, mouvement étapes)  
- `/interviews` (Planification, modification)  
- `/evaluations` (Soumission notes, commentaires)  
- `/notifications` (Lecture, marquage lu)  
- `/analytics` (Statistiques recrutement)  

**Contrôleurs** :  
- `AuthController`  
- `UsersController`  
- `CompaniesController`  
- `JobsController`  
- `CandidatesController`  
- `ApplicationsController`  
- `InterviewsController`  
- `EvaluationsController`  
- `NotificationsController`  
- `AnalyticsController`  

**Services** :  
- `AuthService` (JWT, hashing mots de passe)  
- `UsersService`  
- `CompaniesService`  
- `JobsService`  
- `CandidatesService`  
- `ApplicationsService` (Gestion pipeline)  
- `InterviewsService`  
- `EvaluationsService`  
- `NotificationsService`  
- `AnalyticsService`  

---

## 4. Architecture Frontend et Intégration  
**Outils UI** :  
- React Components :  
  - `Dashboard` (Graphiques, statistiques)  
  - `JobsList` (Recherche, filtres, création offre)  
  - `CandidateProfile` (Tabs: Overview, Resume, Interviews, Evaluations, Activity)  
  - `RecruitmentPipeline` (Kanban : Colonnes Applied → Screening → Shortlisted → Interview → Offer → Hired + Rejected)  
  - `InterviewScheduler` (Calendrier, liste, création/modif)  
  - `EvaluationForm` (Grille notes, sélection recommandation)  
  - `CandidateSearch` (Filtres compétences, statut, expérience)  
  - `Messaging` (WebSocket pour messagerie)  
  - `NotificationsCenter` (Liste, marquage lu)  

**Sécurité** :  
- JWT (Stocké en HttpOnly Cookie)  
- Refresh Tokens (Renouvellement session)  
- CORS (Contrôle accès API)  
- Rate Limiting (Prévention abus)  

**Communication** :  
- REST API (Axios)  
- WebSockets (Socket.IO pour messagerie temps réel)  
- Polling (Mise à jour étapes candidature)  

**Design System** :  
- Couleurs :  
  - Primaire : Bleu (#1976D2)  
  - Success : Vert (#4CAF50)  
  - Warning : Orange (#FF9800)  
  - Danger : Rouge (#F44336)  
- Typographie : Roboto (Titres), Open Sans (Corps)  
- Composants :  
  - Cards (Bordures légères)  
  - Boutons cohérents (Primaire, Secondaire, Danger)  
  - Badges (Statut candidature)  
  - Modals (Création offre, édition candidat)  
  - Tooltips (Infos supplémentaires)  
  - Tabs (Navigation Candidate Profile)  
  - Tables (Liste candidats/offres)  

**États UI** :  
- Loading (Spinners)  
- Empty (Message "Aucune donnée")  
- Error (Toast notifications)  
- Success (Confirmation actions)  

---

## 5. Flux Navigation  
**Recruteur** :  
`Dashboard` → `Jobs` → `Job Details` → `Candidates` → `Candidate Profile` → `Schedule Interview` → `Evaluation` → `Move Candidate` → `Offer` → `Hired`  

**Candidat** :  
`Home` → `Jobs` → `Job Details` → `Apply` → `My Applications` → `Application Tracking` → `Interview` → `Final Decision`  

--- 

**Remarque** : Architecture conçue pour modularité, scalabilité et conformité RGPD (chiffrement données sensibles).